---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How It Works"
  description="Understand how Retenqo captures, processes, stores, and retrieves memories locally on Android."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
    <p
      class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-widest text-[var(--accent-primary)] uppercase"
    >
      Architecture
    </p>
    <h1
      class="mt-3 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-[var(--text-primary)] sm:text-4xl"
    >
      How Retenqo works
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--text-secondary)]">
      Retenqo processes your personal information through a four-stage local
      pipeline on your Android device.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-10 space-y-6">
      <div
        class="rounded-xl border border-[var(--border-subtle)] bg-[var(--bg-secondary)] p-6"
      >
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)]">
          1. Capture (User-Controlled)
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--text-secondary)]">
          You decide what enters Retenqo: opt-in notifications from selected
          apps, screenshots, voice notes, or manual entries. Capture can be
          paused globally at any time.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div
        class="rounded-xl border border-[var(--border-subtle)] bg-[var(--bg-secondary)] p-6"
      >
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)]">
          2. Understand (On-Device AI)
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--text-secondary)]">
          Local OCR and on-device language models extract key entities,
          commitments, and dates without sending your personal text to external
          cloud servers.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div
        class="rounded-xl border border-[var(--border-subtle)] bg-[var(--bg-secondary)] p-6"
      >
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)]">
          3. Remember (Local Storage)
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--text-secondary)]">
          Memories are indexed locally on your device. You can export encrypted
          backups or delete any item permanently.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div
        class="rounded-xl border border-[var(--border-subtle)] bg-[var(--bg-secondary)] p-6"
      >
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)]">
          4. Retrieve (Source-Backed Answers)
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--text-secondary)]">
          Ask natural questions in the assistant. Retenqo retrieves relevant
          memories and shows the exact source behind every answer.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
